**Physical interpretation.** α is the linear screening (mass) coefficient:
it sets the balance between diffusion (−Δ_M) and the restoring force, so
changing α rescales the effective inverse operator (−Δ_M + αI)⁻¹ applied to
the *entire* right-hand side h — a global, first-order effect on every
point. β controls the cubic self-interaction, which only acts where |u| is
appreciable (|u| ≤ {np.abs(u).max():.2f}, so βu³ reaches
